# Daily window in which the panel is switched off -- one line, nothing else.
#
# Copy this to ~/.config/claude-ipixel/off-time.txt and set your own:
#
#     mkdir -p ~/.config/claude-ipixel
#     echo 1:00-6:00 > ~/.config/claude-ipixel/off-time.txt
#
# The panel is dark from the first time (inclusive) to the second
# (exclusive) on the 24-hour clock, and the window may wrap past
# midnight: 23:00-6:00. --off-time 1:00-6:00 on the command line does
# the same thing without a file.
#
# With no such file and no --off-time the panel is never switched off by
# the clock. Blank lines and everything after a # are ignored.

1:00-6:00
